\chapter{Topology of Moral Vortices}

A moral-vortex is defined as a closed circulation in the agency field:

\[
\oint_{\Gamma} \vec{v} \cdot d\ell \neq 0
\]

Its stability is determined by its vorticity magnitude:

\[
\Omega = \nabla \times \vec{v}
\]

Toxic affect loops form when:

\[
\frac{\partial \Omega}{\partial t} &gt; 0 \quad \text{and} \quad \nabla \cdot \vec{v} &lt; 0
\]

meaning agency spirals inward without semantic propagation.

The maximal polarization state corresponds to:

\begin{equation}
|\Omega| \rightarrow 1,\quad \nabla S \rightarrow 0 \quad \text{(static, cyclic outrage state)}
\end{equation}

