\chapter{Information Monopoles and Field Centralization}

An information monopole is defined by field flux imbalance:

\[
\Phi_{\text{out}} = \oint_S \vec{v} \cdot d\vec{A}
\]

For a decentralized system:

\[
\sum_i \Phi_{\text{out},i} = 0
\]

For platform monopolization:

\[
|\Phi_{\text{out,major}}| \gg |\Phi_{\text{out,others}}|
\]

Field collapse occurs when the entropy gradient aligns with the vector potential:

\[
\nabla S \parallel \vec{v}
\]

This eliminates degrees of freedom orthogonal to platform-incentive directions.

