\chapter{LLMs as Low-Curvature Semantic Surfaces}

Semantic curvature is defined as:

\[
\mathcal{K} = \det(\nabla^2 \Phi)
\]

Human discourse exhibits mixed curvature ($\mathcal{K} &gt; 0$ generative regions, $\mathcal{K} &lt; 0$ exploratory regions).

LLMs exhibit:

\[
\mathcal{K}_{LLM} \approx 0
\]

indicating \textit{flat generativity}: high-volume continuation, low semantic acceleration.

The key pathology:

\begin{itemize}
\item High \emph{token entropy}
\item Low \emph{agency entropy}
\item Minimal effective curvature
\end{itemize}

Thus:

\[
\text{LLM output} \equiv \text{semantic foam without gradient}
\]

