\chapter{Group velocity and effective diffusion (RSVP analogues)}

By following the asymptotic derivation in the h-NRCH setting, we obtain RSVP-analog expressions for the anisotropic group velocity $v_g(\psi)$ and effective diffusion $D_{\rm eff}(\psi)$ for transverse perturbations (here $\psi$ is the angle between perturbation wavevector and the reference semantic-wave direction):

\begin{align}
v_g(\psi) &amp;= q_0 \alpha_{\rm A}\!\left(2 - \Gamma_{\rm P} \sin^2\psi\right)\; \frac{\gamma + 2 q_0^2 \rho_0^{-2} \sin^2\psi}{\gamma + \dots}, \label{eq:vg_rsvp}\\
D_{\rm eff}(\psi) &amp;= \gamma q_0^2 \cos^2\psi + q_0^2\sin^2\psi + D_m(\psi), \label{eq:Deff_rsvp}
\end{align}
where $\gamma$ is an Eckhaus-like factor determined by the reference semantic amplitude and pattern wave number, and $D_m(\psi)$ is a cross-diffusion term proportional to $\Gamma_{\rm P}$ arising from coupling to attention flow. The exact coefficients depend on the background pattern $\Phi_0$ and can be computed by the same projection method used in Ref. \cite{pisegna2025nonreciprocal}. The important structural facts are:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $\Gamma_{\rm P}$ produces a wave-number independent contribution to growth/damping analogous to $\lambda_0$ in the h-NRCH model.
  \item For a given $\Gamma_{\rm P}$ there exists a critical semantic wavelength $q_E$ (an RSVP Eckhaus threshold) below which particular perturbation directions destabilize.
  \item Nonreciprocal agency ($\alpha_{\rm A}$) can stabilize otherwise unstable regimes, creating a disorderâ†’ordered transition controlled by $\alpha_{\rm A}/|\Gamma_{\rm P}|$.
\end{enumerate}

Practical implementation: use the same pseudospectral simulation recipe and linear-stability matrix construction as in h-NRCH to compute $\Lambda_0(\psi)$, $v_g(\psi)$ and $D_{\rm eff}(\psi)$ numerically for RSVP parameter choices; see the Supplemental Material of the h-NRCH paper for an explicit algorithm.

