\chapter{Behavioral Capture as Energy Landscape Collapse}

Given a decision-manifold $\mathcal{M}$ with local degrees of freedom $x_i$:

\[
H = \int_{\mathcal{M}} \left( \frac{1}{2} |\nabla \Phi|^2 + V(S) - \vec{v} \cdot \nabla \Phi \right) dV
\]

with potential:

\[
V(S) = \frac{1}{2} k S^2 - \kappa S^3
\]

Behavioral capture imposes a non-linear cubic well, producing three regimes:

\begin{itemize}
\item Stable agency (diverse choices, shallow minima)
\item Competing narratives (multi-minima metastability)
\item Collapse to a capture well (authoritarian attractor)
\end{itemize}

When AI platforms reinforce choices proportional to predicted engagement $E$:

\[
P(\text{choice}) \propto e^{\beta E}
\]

the landscape loses convexity, guaranteeing path-dependent lock-in.

