\chapter{Luhmann's Autopoiesis and RSVP Boundary Dynamics}

Luhmann defines social systems as autopoietic networks of communication that recursively reproduce their own elements through distinction-making operations \cite{luhmann1995social}. In RSVP terms:

\begin{theorem}[Autopoietic Stability]
A meaning system maintains autopoiesis if and only if:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Its communication boundary satisfies $\oint \mathbf{v} \cdot d\mathbf{A} = 0$ (operational closure)
    \item Its internal semantic field maintains $\nabla \Phi &gt; \Phi_c &gt; 0$ (recursive distinction capacity)
\end{enumerate}
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Closure ensures the system defines its own elements (communications) without external determination. Non-vanishing gradients ensure sufficient distinction density for recursive operations. Capture violates both: platform algorithms breach closure while optimization flattens gradients.
\end{proof}

The restoration operators thus serve as autopoietic maintenance mechanisms:
- Divergence sustains distinction capacity
- Circulation enforces closure
- Re-entropization prevents operational stagnation

