Here $D_\Phi$ is semantic diffusivity, $\mathbf{J}(\Phi)$ is a nonreciprocal coupling current (e.g. antisymmetric between topic channels), $\rho$ is an effective inertia of attention (often small; overdamped limit $\rho\to0$ is relevant), $\eta$ a damping coefficient (attention loss), and $\mathbf{Q}$ is an \emph{active stress} tensor that converts semantic gradients into attention flow:
