\chapter{Eckhaus Stability Analysis for Semantic Waves}

Consider a traveling semantic wave solution of the form:
\[
\Phi_0(x,t) = A \cos(q_0 x - \omega t) + \Phi_m
\]
with wave number $q_0$ and frequency $\omega = v_g q_0$.

To determine the stability of this pattern against long-wavelength modulations, we perform an Eckhaus analysis. Let:
\[
\Phi(x,t) = \Phi_0(x,t) + \epsilon \delta\Phi(x,t)
\]
where $\epsilon \ll 1$ and $\delta\Phi$ varies slowly in space and time.

The modulation ansatz is:
\[
\delta\Phi = \hat{\Phi}(X,T) e^{i Q x} + \text{c.c.}, \quad X = \epsilon x, \quad T = \epsilon^2 t
\]
with $|Q| \ll q_0$.

Substituting into the RSVP equations and collecting terms at order $\epsilon$, we obtain the amplitude equation:
\[
\partial_T \hat{\Phi} = \xi_\parallel(Q) \partial_X^2 \hat{\Phi} + \xi_\perp(Q) \hat{\Phi} + g|\hat{\Phi}|^2 \hat{\Phi}
\]

The Eckhaus stability boundary occurs when the parallel diffusion coefficient vanishes:
\[
\xi_\parallel(Q) = 0
\]

For the RSVP-hNRCH system, this yields:
\[
Q_E^2 = \frac{1}{3\xi_0} \left(1 - \frac{\Gamma_{\rm P}}{D_\Phi q_0^2}\right)
\]

Thus the Eckhaus instability threshold is:
\[
\boxed{q_E = \sqrt{\frac{\Gamma_{\rm P}}{D_\Phi \left(1 - 3\xi_0 Q^2\right)}}}
\]

Semantic waves with wave number $q_0 &lt; q_E$ are Eckhaus-unstable and will develop sideband modulations leading to pattern collapse.

