<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{The Necessity of a Restoration Operator}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">From Part 15, the capture operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span></span></span></span> strictly contracts semantic phase volume <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">V</span></span></span></span> and amplifies agency divergence <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î©</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î©</span></span></span></span>.
Therefore, reversal of capture is impossible under endogenous dynamics alone.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">We formalize a \emph{restoration operator} <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span></span></span></span> such that:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">    \rho(\mathcal{R}\mathcal{C}) &lt; 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>â‹…</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">â‹…</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is the spectral radius.
Only under this condition can collapse modes be damped and autonomy restored.</p>
<hr>
