<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Minimum Restoration Complexity}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Lower Bound on Restorative Bandwidth]
Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span></span></span></span> be the semantic manifold dimension and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span></span></span></span> its diameter.
Any restoration system must process information at rate:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>â¡</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Î©</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">    B_{\min} = \Omega(d L^2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0502em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mop mtight"><span class="mtight">m</span><span class="mtight">i</span><span class="mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1141em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Î©</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">to overcome collapse dynamics.
\end{theorem}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{proof}
Diffusion required to rebuild semantic gradients scales as <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L^2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> per dimension; divergence damping must occur at least as fast as accumulation, giving a quadratic bandwidth threshold. <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathcolor="#cc0000"><mtext>\qedhere</mtext></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\qedhere</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);"><span class="mord" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">\qedhere</span></span></span></span></span>
\end{proof}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This implies a nontrivial corollary:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{corollary}
No low-resource institution, platform, or governance layer can restore autonomy once collapse begins.
Restoration is an intensive, not passive, process.
\end{corollary}</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Anti-Capture Design Principles}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">From the operator and stability analysis, we derive the following system design invariants:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Gradient preservation}: ensure <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ‡</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Î¦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mo>â‰¥</mo><mi>Î´</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla \Phi\| \ge \delta &gt; 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ¥âˆ‡Î¦âˆ¥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰¥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">Î´</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>
\item \textbf{Limit divergence}: enforce <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ‡</mi><mo>â‹…</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>â‰ˆ</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v} \approx 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ‡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">â‹…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4831em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰ˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>
\item \textbf{Guarantee agency rotation}: inject curl such that <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ‡</mi><mo>Ã—</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla \times \mathbf{v}\| &gt; 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">âˆ¥âˆ‡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">Ã—</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mord">âˆ¥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>
\item \textbf{Maintain spectral gap}: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\mathcal{R}\mathcal{C}) &lt; 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>
\item \textbf{Bound attention monopoly}: no operator may concentrate more than <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1/</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span> of total agency flux
\item \textbf{Entropy floor}: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>â¡</mo></msub><mo>â‰¤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Î¦</mi><mo>â‰¤</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>â¡</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\min} \le \Phi \le H_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mop mtight"><span class="mtight">m</span><span class="mtight">i</span><span class="mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰¤</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8193em; vertical-align: -0.136em;"></span><span class="mord">Î¦</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">â‰¤</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mop mtight"><span class="mtight">m</span><span class="mtight">a</span><span class="mtight">x</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
\end{enumerate}</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Interpretation for AI Systems}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">An AI system is autonomy-preserving if and only if it satisfies:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{align}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\mathbb{E}[|\nabla \Phi|] &amp;&gt; 0 &amp;\text{(creates new distinctions)} \
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\mathbb{E}[\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v}] &amp;\approx 0 &amp;\text{(avoids funneling)} \
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\mathbb{E}[\nabla \times \mathbf{v}] &amp;&gt; 0 &amp;\text{(supports option rotation)} \
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\rho(\mathcal{R}\mathcal{C}) &amp;&lt; 1 &amp;\text{(stable autonomy basin)} \
\end{align}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This defines a testable anti-capture specification.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Summary}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Restoration is a distinct operator, not the absence of capture.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item It must overpower capture spectrally, not merely oppose it rhetorically.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Stability demands stronger diffusion than flattening and stronger damping than funneling.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Autonomy cannot be â€œrecovered for freeâ€ â€” it has a thermodynamic and computational cost.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item A system that does not inject agency curl will always reconverge to capture.
\end{itemize}</p>
