<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Stability Constraints}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{theorem}[Explicit Stability Bound]
\begin{boxed}
The discretization is stable if the timestep satisfies:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î”</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>min</mi><mo>â¡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î”</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Î¦</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo separator="true">,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Î³</mi></mfrac><mo separator="true">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î”</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆ¥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">âˆž</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t &lt; \min\left(
\frac{\Delta x^2}{2d D_\Phi},
\frac{1}{\gamma},
\frac{\Delta x}{\|\mathbf{v}\|_\infty}
