<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\chapter{Convergence, Chaos, and Field Attractors in Simulation}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\epigraph{``An attractor is a decision fossil.''}{E. Lorenz (rephrased)}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Simulated cognitive fields exhibit one of three regimes:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{enumerate}
