<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\chapter{Semantic Entropy, Novelty, and Manifold Volume}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\epigraph{``Entropy is not the absence of structure, but the presence of unexplored structure.''}{L. da Costa (generalized)}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Semantic entropy is distinct from Shannon entropy on tokens. Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">M</span></span></span></span> be the semantic state manifold. Define the semantic volume:</p>
